<task id="011" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Refactor `IncomingAssociationResolver` → Association Engine over a NORMALIZED ENVELOPE (rung interface + confidence + provenance)</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>10</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>010</dependencies>
    <blocks>012, 013, 014</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, refactoring, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Brownfield refactor of a shared, live server resolver consumed by the inbound pipeline; changes the core association contract (envelope + rung interface) that tasks 012–015 build on; must preserve existing inbound match behavior under test BEFORE extending (R-7); respects ADR-024 / ADR-028 / ADR-045 and bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-serial-spine</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-09</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Refactor the existing `IncomingAssociationResolver` into the **Association Engine**: a rung-based resolver that operates ONLY over a normalized message envelope — NEVER `Microsoft.Graph.Message`. Finalize the `NormalizedMessage` envelope introduced in task 010 to its full shape: `{ direction, from, to[], cc[], subject, bodyText, bodyHtml, internetMessageId, inReplyTo, references[], conversationId, sentAt, attachments[] }`. Introduce a rung interface (e.g. `IAssociationRung` with an ordered `RungOrder`/`RungKind`) so rungs 0–3 (tasks 012–014) and later rungs 4–5 (W3) plug in uniformly, each emitting per-attribute confidence + provenance.

    This is the serial spine of Wave 1: it is `parallel-safe: false` because it refactors the shared resolver that 012/013/014/015 extend. Because it is brownfield, the binding order is: FIRST characterize and preserve the current rungs 0–2 behavior under regression tests, THEN extract the envelope + rung interface, THEN confirm behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged for existing inbound matches (R-7). Do NOT add new rung logic in this task — 012–014 own the rung content. Task 011 delivers the envelope, the rung abstraction, the provenance/confidence model, and a Graph→envelope normalizer, with existing behavior preserved.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer specializing in careful brownfield refactors of live pipelines. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-024 (polymorphic regarding family — engine keeps writing typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields), ADR-028 (central auth; never `new` a credential), ADR-045 (Communication ADR), and the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `IncomingAssociationResolver` is refactored into an Association Engine that consumes only `NormalizedMessage`. A Graph→envelope normalizer maps `Microsoft.Graph.Message` into `NormalizedMessage` at the pipeline boundary. A rung interface + per-attribute confidence + provenance model exists and is documented. Existing inbound matches (rungs 0–2 behavior) are unchanged — proven by regression tests written BEFORE the extraction. Engine emits ADR-024 typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields exactly as before. Build clean; tests green; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Today `IncomingAssociationResolver` is coupled to `Microsoft.Graph.Message` and mixes rung logic inline. R4 needs one engine that works for BOTH directions (inbound + outbound) and future channels, which is only possible if it operates over a channel-neutral envelope (NFR-04 channel extensibility). The spec (FR-09) mandates: envelope-only input, rung interface, per-attribute confidence + provenance, and — critically — rungs 0–2 preserved under test before any extension (risk R-7: silent regression of live inbound matching).

      Task 010 already introduced a `NormalizedMessage` skeleton and swapped enrichment to delegate association to the resolver seam. Task 011 finalizes the envelope, refactors the resolver behind the seam, and adds the normalizer — so 010's delegation now targets the Engine. Tasks 012 (rungs 0–1), 013 (rung 2), 014 (rung 3) implement rung content against the rung interface this task defines.

      ADR-024 constraint: the engine MUST keep writing typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields via the existing `RegardingFieldPriority`/`PopulateResolverFieldsAsync` / `RegardingLookupMap` machinery — this is a refactor of HOW matches are computed, not a change to WHAT gets written.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/NormalizedMessage.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationDirection.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationAssociation.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-09: the Engine MUST operate over the normalized envelope only; it MUST NOT reference `Microsoft.Graph.Message` in rung logic. Graph→envelope mapping happens once, at the boundary.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">R-7 (binding order): characterize + preserve rungs 0–2 behavior under regression tests BEFORE extracting the envelope/rung interface. Existing inbound matches MUST be unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Rung interface + per-attribute confidence + provenance are introduced here; rung CONTENT (0–3) is owned by tasks 012/013/014 — do NOT add new match logic in 011.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Engine MUST keep writing typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields (reuse `RegardingFieldPriority`/`PopulateResolverFieldsAsync`/`RegardingLookupMap`); no new regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject central `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`/canonical Dataverse interfaces; never `new` a credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Association Engine shape is codified in ADR-045 (task 005); confirm alignment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Association remains best-effort/non-fatal within enrichment; the refactor MUST NOT change that invariant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Register any renamed/added services via `CommunicationModule` only (ADR-010); keep DI unconditional (endpoints/processor consume unconditionally, ADR-032).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">bff-extensions Placement Justification REQUIRED in the PR; publish-size delta reported (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/plan.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
