      <file>docs/architecture/email-processing-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/communication-service-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Characterization-tests-before-refactor" location=".claude/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md">
        Lock existing behavior with tests first (KEEP-path categories), then refactor, then re-run to prove no regression (R-7).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="ADR-024 regarding write path" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs">
        `RegardingFieldPriority` + `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync` + `RegardingLookupMap` write typed lookups + denormalized fields. Preserve these outputs verbatim.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Boundary normalization" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs">
        Map the channel-specific message (`Microsoft.Graph.Message`) into `NormalizedMessage` exactly once, at the pipeline boundary; rungs never see Graph types.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `IncomingAssociationResolver.cs` in full; inventory every current rung/match path (explicit ref, thread, participant) and every ADR-024 field it writes. Record the current behavior contract in `notes/011-resolver-behavior-contract.md`.</step>
    <step order="2">Write/extend regression (characterization) tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` that lock the CURRENT rungs 0–2 outputs (matched entity, regarding fields written, denormalized values) for representative inbound fixtures. These MUST pass against the pre-refactor code (R-7 baseline).</step>
    <step order="3">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (§F test obligation, §F.1 asymmetric registration, §G hot-path) and ADR-024 to confirm the regarding write contract before touching it.</step>
    <step order="4">Finalize `NormalizedMessage` (all FR-09 fields: `direction, from, to[], cc[], subject, bodyText, bodyHtml, internetMessageId, inReplyTo, references[], conversationId, sentAt, attachments[]`) with an attachment sub-model.</step>
    <step order="5">Introduce the rung abstraction: `IAssociationRung` (ordered `RungKind`/`RungOrder`, `Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;RungMatch&gt;&gt; EvaluateAsync(NormalizedMessage, context, ct)`) and the `RungMatch` model carrying target entity ref, per-attribute confidence, and provenance fragments. Do NOT implement rung content — provide the abstraction + a thin adapter that wraps the CURRENT inline logic so behavior is preserved (tasks 012–014 replace these with real rungs).</step>
    <step order="6">Add a Graph→envelope normalizer (`GraphMessageNormalizer` or equivalent) mapping `Microsoft.Graph.Message` → `NormalizedMessage`, invoked once at the boundary in `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`. Rung logic references only `NormalizedMessage`.</step>
    <step order="7">Refactor `IncomingAssociationResolver` into the Association Engine: it iterates rungs in order over the envelope, aggregates `RungMatch` results, and writes ADR-024 typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields exactly as before via the existing `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync`/`RegardingLookupMap` machinery. Keep the enrichment seam (task 010) pointing at the Engine.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `CommunicationModule` DI (rename/add registrations; unconditional). Confirm `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` and enrichment (010) compile against the new engine surface.</step>
    <step order="9">Re-run the Step 2 characterization tests — they MUST pass UNCHANGED, proving rungs 0–2 behavior preserved (R-7). Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + full `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-011-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention). Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: invoke `code-review` on the diff; invoke `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus ADR-024 regarding-write preservation + FR-09 envelope-only + R-7). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; serial-spine — confirm no other active worktree is mid-edit in `Services/Communication/`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (011 ✅) and `current-task.md`; unblock 012/013/014; record decisions (envelope shape, rung interface signature, normalizer placement).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
