  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`NormalizedMessage` carries all FR-09 fields (`direction, from, to[], cc[], subject, bodyText, bodyHtml, internetMessageId, inReplyTo, references[], conversationId, sentAt, attachments[]`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Association Engine rung logic references `NormalizedMessage` only — zero references to `Microsoft.Graph.Message` in rung/match code (grep-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Graph→envelope normalizer maps `Microsoft.Graph.Message` → `NormalizedMessage` once at the pipeline boundary.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An `IAssociationRung` abstraction with ordered rungs + a `RungMatch` model (target ref + per-attribute confidence + provenance) exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Characterization tests written BEFORE the refactor pass UNCHANGED after it — rungs 0–2 inbound matches produce identical entity + regarding-field outputs (R-7).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Engine still writes ADR-024 typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields via existing `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync`/`RegardingLookupMap` (no new regarding mechanism).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `new` credential/`ConfidentialClientApplication`; central auth injected (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; Communication tests green; publish-size delta ≈ 0; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This is the serial spine of Wave 1 — it MUST land before 012/013/014 and MUST NOT run concurrently with them. The rung ADAPTER in Step 5 is a temporary wrapper around current inline logic so behavior is preserved; 012–014 replace those adapters with real rungs.

    Do NOT add new match/rung behavior here. If a temptation arises to "just fix" a rung while refactoring, defer it to 012/013/014 to keep R-7's before/after diff clean.

    The behavior-contract note (`notes/011-resolver-behavior-contract.md`) is the reference the rung tasks and task 017 use to write direction-symmetry + per-rung tests.
  </notes>

